ing to be one of the largest market  places in the country currently we're at  about a five billion dollar industry  growing at the fastest pace of any other  industry in the world right now  California alone can can truly actually  triple these numbers what you have to  have is you have to have infrastructure  commoditization of this product is  happening today if you look at what the  nestles of the world needs sugar for  you're finding that if you look at the  numbers in Colorado its  edibles in the consumables market that's  actually outselling the flower two to  one so what you're finding is  commoditization of the flower itself to  produce all of these other goods so you  truly need a fair and orderly  marketplace to do so just like we see in  sugar the fortunate part of what we get  to do is enter a marketplace now before  many participants can and we've brought  a team that can help us extrapolate this  business globally
 

